  "name": "config: default init (no --jira) writes null remotes that 500s slop web",
  "slug": "config-default-init-no-jira-writes-null-remotes-that-500s-sl",
  "spec": {
    "summary": "slop init without --jira writes remotes: as YAML null, which fails config validation in the web data source and 500s every slop web page on the default (no-Jira) setup.",
    "details_md": "Verified: `slop init --yes` (no --jira) emits a bare `remotes:` line (null). `slop status` tolerates it but `GET /tickets` returns HTTP 500. Root fix belongs in the config schema/parser so null/empty remotes coerces to {} and null repo/jira to undefined — covering both init output and hand-edited configs. (Web-side resilience is tracked separately.)",
    "acceptance": [
      "config parsing coerces a null/empty `remotes` to an empty object and null `repo`/`jira` to undefined, so a default `slop init` (no --jira) config validates",
      "slop web serves 200 on all views against a repo created by a plain `slop init` with no jira remote",
      "a test covers the null-remotes config parsing"
    ],
    "context": [
      "src/core/entities/config.ts (configSchema)",
      "src/cli/config-yaml.ts (parse)",
      "repro: init --yes (no --jira) -> GET /tickets HTTP 500"
    ],
